"## Summary\n\nDevstack follow-up 36: D-162 in the fixture, so the lab's regular node reports observations every 5 s. Also the audit of every consumer that cadence can touch, and one full acceptance run on agent-core 51 and updater 26.\n- **Session:** launched 09:06 EST on 2026-11-04 on #473's roadmap row `52b93845`, and delivered at 10:22.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 4 commits and 125 owned files, +13,750/−10. Most of it is the run's records under `docs/e2e/runs/2026-11-04/followup36/`.\n  - **The code:** one line in `tests/e2e/cmd/fvpn-e2e-prepare/main.go`, `\"observation_seconds\": 5`, with a TEST ONLY comment naming D-162.\n  - **Supporting changes:**\n    - the installer node's existing override is moved, unchanged, into `installerServingConfig` (`tests/e2e/installer_config.go`);\n    - offline tests for both;\n    - the evidence-hygiene test now includes `followup36`.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merge-tree clean on current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes.\n  - **The orchestrator reran these** on a scratch tree: current `main` after isolation 24 (#475, `2a7065b7`) with this branch merged in. All pass:\n    - `make -f mk/e2e.mk e2e-lint` and `make -f mk/at-isolation.mk at-isolation-lint`;\n    - `go vet -tags e2e ./tests/e2e/...` and `go test ./tests/e2e/...`, including the new prepared-config and installer-config tests;\n    - `go test ./tests/handover/...`, and the committed-evidence tests (`TestCommitted*` in `tests/netlab`, `tests/e2e` and `tests/e2e/at/...`);\n    - `make go-lint`, gofmt and `git diff --check`;\n    - the scheduled job's evaluator on the run's committed summary: PASS, exit 0.\n- **Scope:** one full acceptance run, with no rerun and no reservation. Admission waits totalled 32 minutes, none inside a timed section. All 286 host samples were free of foreign overlap. Zero owned Docker objects at the end. No AT lane, product code, contract or nightly-list entry changed.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **D-162, TEST ONLY.** Both prepared configs, `agent-enroll.json` and `agent-run.json`, now carry heartbeat, poll and observation at 5 s.\n  - The product default stays 30 s, and every predicate stays as it was, the 15 s freshness bound included.\n  - The installer node already reported every 5 s. Its values are unchanged, and a test pins them.\n- **The run:** `c17589fa`, on `f6edbda9`, which is `main` at `52b93845` plus this branch's code. 14:32:49–14:56:48Z, 1,439.3 s.\n  - **32 pass, 1 blocked (`member-ipv6`), 0 fail.** Make exits 2. The unchanged nightly evaluator passes, exit 0.\n  - **Every scenario's status matches follow-up 35's.**\n- **The cadence, from the stack's database before teardown:**\n  - 123 accepted regular-node observations in the run's window, so 122 intervals between successive `received_at`;\n  - **min 0.081 s, median 5.162 s, max 10.255 s.** Forty intervals are 9 s or longer, and none is discarded. Reports also go out on a state change, so 5 s is a setting, not a period;\n  - the last accepted row is at 14:46:26.20Z, 1.7 s before `lease-expiry` stopped the control plane. So the run's last 622 s had none.\n- **The 15 s reads: none ran.** The acceptance path does not call `servingGate26` or `survivorHold30`, and their opt-in campaigns were skipped.\n  - **So this run does not re-score F22-D146.** Members 23's dual 1280 rows still need their owner's run under D-162.\n- **The `If-Match` side effect.** The run exercised three node writes: the capacity PATCH, the publication PUT and the node revocation POST.\n  - Each got 202 on its first attempt, with **zero 412s**.\n  - Every owned writer already uses the shared bounded retry in `tests/e2e/node_write.go`, from follow-ups 32 and 33, so none was added.\n- **The consumer audit** is a table in `analysis.md`, by file and line, for every acceptance consumer of the regular node's observation freshness, cadence or count, and for every `If-Match` writer.\n  - **One missing retry, outside this lane:** isolation's operator-assist capacity PATCH (`tests/e2e/at/isolation/assist.py:22`) makes a single GET/`If-Match` attempt. It is routed to isolation.\n  - The other AT lanes' consumers are routed with what each must keep.\n- **`update-good`: exit 0, after a 446 ms lock wait.**\n  - **Its one output line is the wait record:** `waited_ms: 446`, `acquired: true`, `budget_ms: 10000`.\n  - **The lock samples show the running agent,** PID 894, holding `update.lock` twice within the wait. The updater, PID 186378, held it next.\n  - **Follow-up 35's acquisition was uncontended,** so this is the first devstack run to record D-158's wait. The wait worked as specified.\n  - **Then the candidate:**\n    - PID 189738 started at 14:45:54.58Z, under its parent's lock;\n    - it reported `recovery_required`, so its boot recovery was deferred;\n    - the parent's lock was gone by 14:45:59.997Z, and the deferral had cleared by 14:46:04.707Z;\n    - its first serving heartbeat was written at 14:46:05.437Z.\n  - **Stale-then-live contention is unobserved.** The samples keep no lock metadata, and no contention was staged.\n- **`update-bad`:** exit 1, `HASH_MISMATCH: artifact`, with no wait record.\n- **`lease-expiry`:** pass, as in 35.\n  - Counted flow came after 2.34 s, and the control stop completed at 14:46:27.87Z.\n  - D, the signed desired policy's expiry, was 14:56:25.26Z. The rule poll saw 558 → 0 member accept rules, and the first closed heartbeat was written 249 ms after D.\n  - With senders still active, replies and byte counters stayed flat. The control restart was ready at 14:56:34.62Z.\n- **Attribution.** This is the first run with agent-core 51, updater 26 and D-162 together. The lane credits no change to any one of them, and that is right.\n- **Carried:** `member-ipv6` stays listed. AT29's guest-clock rollback stays an operator-run row.\n- **Next:**\n  - members 24 runs the dual 1280 rows under D-162;\n  - isolation takes the assist script's retry in a later follow-up, after isolation 25